## Citations

Every claim in `finding.md`'s "Comparison vs literature" section MUST resolve to
a citation here. Each citation block records author, year, edition, ISBN (where
applicable), and the specific page / equation / table being referenced.

### Primary source

- **Author, Year.** *Title*, Nth ed. Publisher. ISBN.
  - Section X.Y, p. ZZZ: <one-line summary of the claim>
  - Equation (X.Y): <restated equation>
  - Table X.Y: <range or coefficient cited>

### Secondary / corroborating

- **Author, Year.** *Title*, Nth ed. Publisher. ISBN.
  - Section X.Y, p. ZZZ: <one-line summary>

### Disagreements / ambiguity

If sources disagree, list each below with the disagreement. A persistent
unresolved disagreement maps to a `LITERATURE-AMBIGUOUS` terminal status.

- <citation A> says <claim>; <citation B> says <conflicting claim>.
  Provisional resolution: <which side this finding chose, or note that the
  disagreement is recorded but not adjudicated>.

